# Task Scheduler Enhancement Plan

This plan outlines several non-breaking improvements to the task-scheduler project to make it more professional, useful, and visually appealing.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Edit Flow Change**: I propose changing the edit functionality to use a modal/dialog. Currently, it deletes the task and fills the main form, which can lead to data loss if not saved.
> - **Data Schema Change**: Adding a `priority` field to tasks. Existing tasks will default to "Média".

## Proposed Changes

### UI & UX Improvements
- **Search Bar**: Add a search input to the header to filter tasks by title/description in real-time.
- **Task Priority**: Add a priority selector (Baixa, Média, Alta) when creating/editing tasks. Cards will show a colorful tag.
- **Task Count Badges**: Show the number of tasks in each Kanban column header.
- **Dark Mode**: Add a sleek dark mode toggle.
- **Confirmation Modals**: Add a confirmation step before deleting a task.

### Code Refactoring
#### [MODIFY] [view.js](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/view.js)
- Update [renderBaseHTML](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/view.js#7-58) to include search bar and dark mode toggle.
- Update [renderTaskList](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/view.js#69-101) to show priority tags and task counts.
- Add methods for handling the search input and priority selection.
- Implement a simple modal for editing.

#### [MODIFY] [controller.js](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/controller.js)
- Add `handleSearch` logic.
- Update [handleEditTask](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/controller.js#58-69) to use the new modal/update flow.
- Update [handleDrop](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/controller.js#90-94) to maintain priority and other data.

#### [MODIFY] [model.js](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/model.js)
- Ensure [updateTask](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/js/model.js#24-31) is used correctly for edits instead of delete+add.

#### [MODIFY] [style.css](file:///home/daniel/Downloads/task-scheduler/src/css/style.css)
- Add styles for priority tags, search bar, dark mode, and modals.
- Enhance animations and transitions for a "premium" feel.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- This project doesn't have a test suite yet. I will manually verify all features.

### Manual Verification
1. **Search**: Type in the search bar and verify tasks filter instantly.
2. **Priority**: Create a task with "Alta" priority and check if the red tag appears.
3. **Edit**: Edit a task title and verify it updates in the column without changing its position (unless status changed).
4. **Drag and Drop**: Verify tasks can still be moved between columns.
5. **Persistence**: Refresh the page and ensure all tasks (with priorities) and the theme preference are saved.
6. **Dark Mode**: Toggle theme and verify all elements adapt correctly.
